## 13. Common Pitfalls

| Pitfall | What happens | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Space is part of the token | `"hello"` and `" hello"` have different IDs | Be consistent about spaces in prompts and training text |
| Trailing space in a prompt | Breaks natural token boundaries and can hurt generation | Avoid trailing spaces |
| Numbers tokenized inconsistently | Model struggles with arithmetic | Split digits |
| Training the tokenizer on tiny data | Poor merges, weak compression | Use a large, representative sample |
| Tokenizer/model mismatch | Garbage output | Always ship the exact tokenizer file with the model |
| Not handling invalid UTF-8 on decode | Crashes | Use `errors="replace"` |
| Special tokens split by BPE | The model never sees the marker as one unit | Split on special tokens before BPE |
| Changing tokenizer after pretraining | Embeddings no longer match | Decide before training starts |
| Ignoring non-English text | Those users pay more and get worse results | Include and up-sample those languages |
| Comparing tokenizers by loss per token | Misleading | Use loss per byte |

